# Environment variables for kolscanhispano.fun.
#
# Real values live only in .env.local, which is gitignored and never echoed,
# logged, or pasted on a command line. This file documents the shape only.

# 32-byte, base64-encoded keys. They live in the host environment (Vercel)
# and never in the database (Neon): a database dump alone must not yield
# addresses. See SECURITY.md.
WALLET_ENC_KEY=
WALLET_HMAC_KEY=

# Base64url secret used to verify Helius webhook deliveries.
HELIUS_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Optional. Enables the Helius DAS fallback in prices.ts, which is the only
# way a mint DexScreener has never heard of ever acquires a symbol. Absent,
# that lookup is a documented no-op and those rows keep symbol = NULL --
# degraded, not broken. Costs 10 credits per mint against a 1,000,000/month
# free tier, which is why scripts/refresh-token-metadata.ts bounds both how
# many mints one run resolves and how often a symbol-less one is re-asked.
HELIUS_API_KEY=

# Optional. How many mints scripts/refresh-token-metadata.ts resolves in one
# run. Unset means its default of 30 -- one DexScreener request's worth. 0 is
# a real value and stops the step doing anything, with no edit and no deploy.
TOKEN_METADATA_LIMIT=

# Neon Postgres connection strings. Both must carry sslmode=verify-full, and
# this is enforced rather than documented: resolveConnectionString() refuses a
# string without it, because nothing in this repo passes an ssl option and the
# text of the secret is therefore the only thing that decides whether the
# connection is encrypted and verified.
#
# DATABASE_URL points at the "production" branch, TEST_DATABASE_URL at the
# "tests" branch. The test suite refuses to run if these two are equal.
#
# Migrating production is `npm run db:migrate -- --prod`. The flag is required:
# no flag used to mean production, which made the shortest command in the repo
# the only one that applied DDL without first asserting anything about its
# target.
DATABASE_URL=
TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# The "preview" Neon branch, a child of "production" created with its data.
# Loaded into Vercel as DATABASE_URL for Preview deployments only, so a preview
# never writes to production -- and never to the "tests" branch, which the suite
# truncates.
#
# `npm run db:seed:preview` is the one piece of local tooling that reads this
# name, and it reads nothing else: it refuses to run if this is unset, if
# DATABASE_URL is unset, if the two name the same database, or if the target
# carries test_database_marker.
#
# The seed writes only `trade` rows and the dirty `position` marks that go with
# them; `position`, `pnl_daily` and `pnl_position_daily` are then derived from
# those trades by the real engine, in a child process running
# `scripts/recompute-dirty.ts` with DATABASE_URL set to *this* branch. The
# variable below is still the only target name it ever reads.
# Apply migrations here too when a branch adds one: `npm run db:migrate:preview`.
# A preview deployment reads this branch, so a schema left behind fails at runtime.
PREVIEW_DATABASE_URL=
